Gives each frame the browser's own ad blocker's agent (//browser_core/ad_block_page_agent.h),
which hides what the page's filters hide and runs their scriptlets as each document starts, from
what the browser sends it before the document commits (#2111). The scriptlets run where
extensions' document_start scripts do, since Blink forbids script while it announces the
document's element. It watches a document's classes and ids, for the generic rules that hide by
them, in an isolated world of its own, which Chrome's list of them gains. It does nothing until the
browser sends it something, which it does only with --ad-block-engine=native.

